blocks.t:
\frac{d\sigma}{dz}
 = -\left(1+e^{-z}\right)^{-2}\cdot\left(-e^{-z}\right)
 = \frac{e^{-z}}{\left(1+e^{-z}\right)^{2}} .

p=\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}}
 \Longrightarrow 
 \frac{1}{p}=1+e^{-z}
 \Longrightarrow 
 e^{-z}=\frac{1-p}{p}
 \Longrightarrow 
 \boxed{ z=\ln \left(\frac{p}{1-p}\right) }

blocks.cap:
The same fitted model, two views. The probability is a curve in $x$;
 the log-odds are a straight line. Logistic regression is linear regression —
 on the log-odds scale.

blocks.t:
\sigma(z)=
 \begin{cases}
 \dfrac{1}{1+e^{-z}} & z\ge0 \quad(\text{then } e^{-z}\le1)
[8pt]
 \dfrac{e^{z}}{1+e^{z}} & z<0 \quad(\text{then } e^{z}<1)
 \end{cases}
